1
00:00:04,299 --> 00:00:08,242
This is Gateline, a retail media platform for airport screens.

2
00:00:08,292 --> 00:00:14,489
It puts the right offer on the right screen, for the passengers actually standing in front of it.

3
00:00:14,539 --> 00:00:18,547
We are at Meridian International, a fictional two-terminal hub.

4
00:00:18,597 --> 00:00:21,702
Every feed is mocked in its real industry format:

5
00:00:21,752 --> 00:00:27,949
AODB flight movements, IATA AIDX messages, and ACI ACRIS queue data, each behind its own adapter.

6
00:00:28,610 --> 00:00:31,834
The platform admin sees the whole network at a glance.

7
00:00:31,884 --> 00:00:35,472
One hundred and eighty-two screens, each coloured by health,

8
00:00:35,522 --> 00:00:39,049
with a heat overlay showing where passengers are right now.

9
00:00:39,099 --> 00:00:43,535
Below, passenger presence is broken down per zone, in five-minute windows:

10
00:00:43,585 --> 00:00:48,930
how many people, which nationalities, where they are flying, and how long they will stay.

11
00:00:49,582 --> 00:00:51,953
Here is the screen at Gate forty-two.

12
00:00:52,003 --> 00:00:58,104
It is showing Saffron Gulf's business upgrade, because flight XY501 is in its boarding window,

13
00:00:58,154 --> 00:01:01,048
and an airline gets priority at its own gate.

14
00:01:01,098 --> 00:01:06,022
Beside the ad is a live departures strip, and a promo code with a countdown.

15
00:01:06,678 --> 00:01:07,994
Now, cause and effect.

16
00:01:08,044 --> 00:01:14,328
In split-screen mode, with the airline view on the right, I inject a forty-five minute delay on XY501.

17
00:01:14,378 --> 00:01:17,495
An IATA AIDX message goes through the feed adapter.

18
00:01:17,545 --> 00:01:23,642
In under a second, the airline sees the delay, and the gate screen switches to duty-free fragrance.

19
00:01:23,692 --> 00:01:25,505
The retailer's rule has fired:

20
00:01:25,555 --> 00:01:30,348
a Gulf flight, delayed more than thirty minutes, at gates forty to forty-five.

21
00:01:31,008 --> 00:01:32,911
Every decision can be explained.

22
00:01:32,961 --> 00:01:36,024
Why this ad shows the crowd in front of the screen:

23
00:01:36,074 --> 00:01:39,503
fifty-eight percent holiday, thirty-one percent families.

24
00:01:39,553 --> 00:01:42,371
Then the top three candidates and their scores.

25
00:01:42,421 --> 00:01:49,146
The AI proposed this ranking, but it only played after deterministic checks confirmed that every cited fact exi

26
00:01:49,196 --> 00:01:53,418
sts in a trusted feed, is fresh, and that the score can be reproduced.

27
00:01:54,074 --> 00:01:55,719
A passenger scans the code.

28
00:01:55,769 --> 00:02:01,807
The claim page shows the offer, with a countdown tied to the moment their flight closes boarding.

29
00:02:01,857 --> 00:02:06,074
They share a second code with family, then redeem it at the counter.

30
00:02:06,728 --> 00:02:12,173
And the redemption lands on the retailer's dashboard straight away, next to live impressions,

31
00:02:12,223 --> 00:02:17,668
scans and conversion, and a forecast of passenger flow near the store for the next two hours.

32
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:20,589
Retailers build campaigns themselves.

33
00:02:20,639 --> 00:02:26,606
As they pick zones and audience weights, a live preview estimates how well they match the crowd,

34
00:02:26,656 --> 00:02:31,620
the expected impressions and redemptions, and the best three slots for tomorrow.

35
00:02:33,295 --> 00:02:39,522
The creative assistant turns a one-line brief into a ready ad page, in English and Kiswahili,

36
00:02:39,572 --> 00:02:41,075
with no API key needed.

37
00:02:44,081 --> 00:02:49,412
The media manager sees every screen and every hour, priced from predicted footfall,

38
00:02:49,462 --> 00:02:51,617
with a seven-day revenue forecast.

39
00:02:51,667 --> 00:02:55,701
A conflict view explains exactly why one campaign beat another.

40
00:02:56,353 --> 00:03:00,106
Airlines see their own flights and can automate delay goodwill.

41
00:03:00,156 --> 00:03:05,719
When a departure runs late past a threshold, a meal voucher, co-funded with a coffee partner,

42
00:03:05,769 --> 00:03:08,013
is pushed to the screens at that gate.

43
00:03:08,666 --> 00:03:13,800
If the AI ever cites something that is not in a trusted feed, the verifier rejects it.

44
00:03:13,850 --> 00:03:19,046
The screen falls back to the rule-based choice, and an incident is raised for the team.

45
00:03:19,697 --> 00:03:25,702
The whole interface switches to Kiswahili in one click, and the product is fully white-label.

46
00:03:25,752 --> 00:03:30,780
Targeting is aggregated by flight, zone and time window only, never by person.

47
00:03:30,830 --> 00:03:32,277
This has been Gateline.
